# struct statfs for the volume the machine runs from, as statfs64("/") wrote it.
#
# Machine   devthrottle-mac-mini, Apple M4, macOS 26.5.2 (build 25F84), arm64
# Taken     2026-11-06
# Call      statfs64("/", buffer) returning 0, 2168 bytes written
#
# What the machine itself reported for the same volume, read at the documented offsets:
#   f_fstypename   (offset   72, 16 bytes)   apfs
#   f_mntonname    (offset   88, 1024 bytes) /
#   f_mntfromname  (offset 1112, 1024 bytes) /dev/disk3s1s1
#
# Only f_mntfromname is read by the probe. The narrowed mission has no per-volume figures and no free
# space; this one field answers which physical disk the machine runs from, which is what
# DiskEvidence.IsInSystemVolume needs. The only readable text anywhere in the record is "apfs" and the
# device name, so it carries nothing private into a public repository.
